WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.675
Two documented incidents
show why this is a

2
00:00:02.675 --> 00:00:05.738
security property and not
a reporting preference.

3
00:00:05.738 --> 00:00:09.727
In 2023, an attacker used a
Microsoft consumer signing

4
00:00:09.727 --> 00:00:13.362
key to forge tokens and
read Exchange Online mail.

5
00:00:13.362 --> 00:00:18.095
The Cyber Safety Review Board counted
22 enterprise organizations affected,

6
00:00:18.095 --> 00:00:20.425
and called the intrusion preventable.

7
00:00:20.425 --> 00:00:24.050
The forged tokens were valid to
every system that checked them.

8
00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:26.729
What caught it was a
custom alert one federal

9
00:00:26.729 --> 00:00:29.625
department had built on
mailbox logs it paid for.

10
00:00:29.625 --> 00:00:33.475
The agency's own evidence found what
the provider's platform didn't.

11
00:00:33.475 --> 00:00:35.537
The second sits beneath the guest.

12
00:00:35.537 --> 00:00:39.329
In February 2023, the ESXiArgs campaign

13
00:00:39.329 --> 00:00:43.925
compromised more than
3,800 VMware ESXi servers.

14
00:00:43.925 --> 00:00:46.866
And Microsoft noted that
many security products

15
00:00:46.866 --> 00:00:49.950
have limited visibility
into the hypervisor at all.

16
00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:52.900
Both cases make the same
point from opposite ends.

17
00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:56.637
The worst failures happened where no
single platform's tool was looking.

18
00:00:56.637 --> 00:00:59.000
There's a consequence for the fix, too.

19
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:03.268
Once one plane names and identifies
everything the agency runs,

20
00:01:03.268 --> 00:01:05.925
it's a complete map of the attack surface.

21
00:01:05.925 --> 00:01:11.094
So the decision: govern that unified plane
as a Tier 0 asset from the day it exists,

22
00:01:11.094 --> 00:01:15.089
with time-boxed administration,
its own monitored telemetry,

23
00:01:15.089 --> 00:01:17.987
and a design that assumes
it will be attacked.

24
00:01:17.987 --> 00:01:22.212
Identity engineering and
the DNS and DDI team own it.

25
00:01:22.212 --> 00:01:24.100
Next, why programs stall.
